DESCRIPTION:Gaming\, Summer Reading\, Tweens\n\nTo ensure fair access for 
 as many families as possible\, please read the registration guidelines for
  this program.One Session Per Week: Patrons may register for only one sess
 ion of this program per week.Duplicate Registrations: Registrations for mo
 re than one session in the same week will be cancelled.We appreciate your 
 understanding as we work to provide equitable access to this popular progr
 am.Get ready to brawl! Join us for an epic Super Smash Bros. Ultimate Tour
 nament on the Nintendo Switch\, where teens battle it out for bragging rig
 hts and prizes. Whether you're a seasoned fighter or a casual button-mashe
 r\, this tournament is open to all skill levels. Come solo or bring your c
 rew—only one will be crowned Smash Champion!We’ll kick things off with
  warm-up rounds\, then dive into a bracket-style tournament with 1v1 match
 es on the big screen. Between matches\, enjoy snacks\, cheer on your frien
 ds\, and hang out in a chill\, gamer-friendly space.Registration for Tween
  Video Gaming: Super Smash Bros. will open at 9:00AM on Wednesday\, July 2
 2nd for Manheim Township and East Lampeter residents and on Wednesday\, Ju
 ly 29th for residents of other municipalities.Library Program PoliciesNo S
 how – Patrons failing to cancel their registration for more than 2 libra
 ry programs in a month will be restricted from registering for future prog
 rams for a period of one month’s time. Please cancel your registrations 
 at least 2 hours prior to the start of the program to allow for those on t
 he waiting list to be notified of their change in registration status.Drop
  Off Program – This program is intended for children from ages 10 to 12 
 years who can participate independently. Adult(s) must be present to check
  in child with youth services staff prior to program. Adults will not be a
 llowed in the event space. Late Arrivals – Please arrive 10 minutes prio
 r to the start of the program to allow for parking and other circumstances
 . The program will begin promptly at the designated time. At this time\, y
 our spot will be forfeited to those on the wait list who will be granted e
 ntry. If spots remain\, registrants may be allowed into the program. Howev
 er\, registrants will not be permitted to enter the program 5 minutes past
  the start time.Check In - All participants must provide an emergency cont
 act number upon registration or at the start of the program.Designated Age
 s – Please adhere to the age restrictions designated on your registrat
 ion. Only children in that age range will be admitted.   Cancellations
 - Please check your email prior to departing to verify that the program ha
 s not been cancelled.
LOCATION:Manheim Township\, MTP Morgan Center C
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/tween-video-gaming-super
 -smash-bros-178990
