BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:American Disasters
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261009T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261009T140000
UID:e88a400db4465f2f160f4662340e6958@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Discussion\, Presentation\, Adults\, Seniors\n\nBest for adult
 s and older interested teens. Registration is appreciated but not required
  if space allows.American Disasters is a six-session PowerPoint series. Dr
 . Robert Frick\, historian and presenter\, will share the stories and fact
 s related to six events that significantly impacted the United States. The
  stories of the Great Chicago Fire of 1871\, the Johnstown Flood of 1889\,
  the San Francisco Earthquake of 1906\, Hurricane Agnes in the Susquehanna
  Basin in 1972\, the Asian Flu Pandemic of 1957-58\, and the Sinking of th
 e USS Indianapolis will be shared during this program. Participants should
  prepare for lively presentations filled with interesting facts and pepper
 ed with humor. Dr. Frick’s goal is education with a smile.
LOCATION:Quarryville\, QVL C.X. Carlson Cultural Room
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/american-disasters-16636
 6
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
